  "global_assumptions": {
    "domain": "Real coefficients, parameters and roots; sign, order and ratio statements use real numbers.",
    "units": "No physical quantities or units are specified; all values are dimensionless.",
    "branches": "Retain every admissible real branch. No physical branch selection is applicable.",
    "equivalence": "Equivalent algebraic proofs and any nonzero real scalar multiple of a constructed quadratic are acceptable.",
    "schema": "Internal mathematical ledger only; no publisher schema gate or final interaction keys."
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "number": 1043,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1043",
          "domain": "b in R; x in R.",
          "result": "Exactly one positive and one negative root for every real b.",
          "roots": ["(-b + sqrt(b^2 + 644))/14", "(-b - sqrt(b^2 + 644))/14"],
          "derivation": [
            "The leading coefficient is 7, so the equation never degenerates.",
            "D = b^2 + 644 > 0, hence two distinct real roots exist.",
            "Their product is -23/7 < 0, so neither is zero and their signs differ.",
            "Equivalently, sqrt(b^2 + 644) > abs(b) makes the plus branch positive and the minus branch negative."
          ],
          "degeneracy": "No exceptional real b."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 1044,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1044",
          "domain": "a in R; x in R.",
          "result": "There is no positive root for any real a; zero is not a root either.",
          "derivation": [
            "For x >= 0, 12*x^2 + 70*x + a^2 + 1 > 0 because a^2 + 1 >= 1.",
            "D = 4852 - 48*a^2 = 4*(1213 - 12*a^2).",
            "When a^2 < 1213/12 there are two distinct negative real roots: (-35 +/- sqrt(1213 - 12*a^2))/12.",
            "When a^2 = 1213/12 there is a repeated negative root -35/12.",
            "When a^2 > 1213/12 there are no real roots."
          ],
          "degeneracy": "Leading coefficient 12 is fixed. 'No positive root' does not assert the existence of real roots."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 1045,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1045",
          "domain": "b in R; two ordered real roots with larger minus smaller = 1/6.",
          "result": "b = -5 or b = 5.",
          "branches": [
            {"b": "-5", "roots_smaller_first": ["1/3", "1/2"]},
            {"b": "5", "roots_smaller_first": ["-1/2", "-1/3"]}
          ],
          "derivation": [
            "For a quadratic with leading coefficient 6, the root separation is sqrt(D)/6.",
            "sqrt(b^2 - 24)/6 = 1/6 gives D = 1, then b^2 = 25.",
            "Both b = -5 and b = 5 yield real roots separated by 1/6 and product 1/6."
          ],
          "degeneracy": "The nonzero prescribed separation excludes a repeated root. Negative roots are not excluded by the wording."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 1046,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1046-a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "domain": "c in R; root separation 0.8 = 4/5.",
          "result": "c = 5.",
          "roots_smaller_first": ["1/5", "1"],
          "derivation": [
            "Vieta gives root sum 30/25 = 6/5.",
            "Together with separation 4/5, the roots are (6/5 +/- 4/5)/2, namely 1 and 1/5.",
            "Their product is 1/5, so c = 25*(1/5) = 5."
          ],
          "degeneracy": "Swapping the root labels changes no coefficient; the roots are distinct and positive."
        },
        {
          "id": "1046-b",
          "source_label": "б",
          "domain": "b in R; two nonzero real roots can be labelled (3*t/2, t), with ratio 1.5 = 3/2.",
          "result": "b = -50 or b = 50.",
          "branches": [
            {"b": "-50", "ratio_ordered_roots": ["5/4", "5/6"]},
            {"b": "50", "ratio_ordered_roots": ["-5/4", "-5/6"]}
          ],
          "derivation": [
            "Vieta gives (3*t/2)*t = 25/24, hence t^2 = 25/36 and t = +/- 5/6.",
            "The root sum is 5*t/2 = +/- 25/12.",
            "b = -24*(root sum), yielding -50 and 50.",
            "The statement does not designate 'larger root divided by smaller root', so both same-sign branches are retained."
          ],
          "degeneracy": "Constant term 25 makes both roots nonzero; ratio 3/2 excludes equality. A positive ratio allows two negative roots."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 1047,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1047",
          "domain": "c in R; two real roots whose squared values differ by 1.75 = 7/4.",
          "result": "c = 6.",
          "roots": ["-2", "-3/2"],
          "squared_difference_order": ["-2", "-3/2"],
          "derivation": [
            "Vieta gives r1 + r2 = -7/2.",
            "Choose labels with r1^2 - r2^2 = 7/4. Then (r1-r2)*(-7/2) = 7/4, so r1-r2 = -1/2.",
            "Solving the sum and difference gives r1 = -2 and r2 = -3/2.",
            "r1*r2 = 3 = c/2, hence c = 6.",
            "Reversing the square-difference order merely swaps the two roots and gives the same c."
          ],
          "degeneracy": "The fixed sum is nonzero, so division by it is valid. D = 49 - 8*c = 1 at the solution."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 1048,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1048",
          "domain": "b,c in R; roots are 4/3 and the literal coefficient b.",
          "result": "b = -1, c = -4.",
          "roots": ["4/3", "-1"],
          "derivation": [
            "The second coefficient of 3*x^2 + b*x + c is b, not -b or -b/3.",
            "Vieta gives 4/3 + b = -b/3; multiplying by 3 gives 4 + 3*b = -b, so b = -1.",
            "c/3 = (4/3)*b, hence c = 4*b = -4.",
            "The resulting polynomial factors as (3*x-4)*(x+1)."
          ],
          "degeneracy": "Leading coefficient 3 is fixed; the coefficient equation is linear with nonzero coefficient 4."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 1049,
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1049",
          "domain": "a,c in R; a > 0 and c != 0; roots are a and c.",
          "result": "a = 1, c = 4.",
          "roots": ["1", "4"],
          "derivation": [
            "Vieta gives a+c = 5/a and a*c = c/a.",
            "Because a > 0 and c != 0, multiply the product relation by a and divide by c to obtain a^2 = 1.",
            "The positivity condition selects a = 1.",
            "The sum relation then gives c = 4; x^2 - 5*x + 4 = (x-1)*(x-4)."
          ],
          "excluded_branches": [
            "a = -1 would give c = -4, but violates a > 0.",
            "If c = 0 were allowed, the separate branch a = sqrt(5), c = 0 would satisfy the root statement with a > 0; it is explicitly excluded.",
            "a = 0 is excluded and would make the equation linear rather than quadratic."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 1050,
      "construction": "For each pair, lambda*(y-y1)*(y-y2) = 0 with any lambda in R excluding 0. The listed equations are convenient representatives.",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "1050-a",
          "source_label": "а",
          "roots": ["10", "12"],
          "sum": "22",
          "product": "120",
          "equation": "y^2 - 22*y + 120 = 0",
          "coefficient_vector": ["1", "-22", "120"]
        },
        {
